Description: Size the expanded -r/-R rule buffer from its inputs to prevent a heap overflow
 expand_rule() expands a -r or -R rule into a fixed RULE_LENGTH (1024) byte
 heap buffer.  The length check in main.c only tests the raw argument of
 the separate "-r RULE" form: the joined "-rRULE" form and -R are
 not checked, and each %f expands to the source file name, so a short rule can
 still overflow.  Reproduced with AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow write
 at utils.c, expand_rule.
 .
 The buffer is now allocated for the rule with every '%' expanded to the source
 name.  Output is unchanged; the existing RULE_LENGTH check is left in place.
Author: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1155614
Forwarded: https://bugs.debian.org/1155614
Last-Updated: 2026-11-28
